<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33903" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">păro</span></b> , āre,
			v. a.
		par, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to make equal</i>, <i>esteem equal.</i>
			* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">eodem hercle vos pono et paro: parissumi estis
					iibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Curc. 4, 2, 20</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In
			partic., <i>to bring to an agreement</i>, <i>arrange</i> with any one: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">se paraturum cum collegā,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Fam. 1, 9, 25</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Fest. p. 234</span></i> Müll.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
